# Security invariants

This Cursor rule supplements the repository AGENTS.md instructions. It may add scoped requirements but may not weaken root security invariants.

**Authority:** root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) §3 · [`docs/SECURITY.md`](../../docs/SECURITY.md)

## Do not

- Put passwords, mnemonics, seeds, private keys, encryption keys, or decrypted vaults outside the crypto worker
- Put secrets in React state, Zustand, localStorage, URLs, logs, clipboard history, analytics, or error reports
- Sign or broadcast without `openSignConfirmDialog`
- Silently change vault formats, KDF/crypto params, derivation paths, worker contracts, persistence, or security boundaries
- Use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or `eval`
- Put crypto logic in `apps/web` or React/Zustand deps in `@hd-wallet/core`
- Persist the session store

When instructions conflict, follow the stricter security-preserving rule and report the conflict.

## Pattern anchors

### BAD

```ts
// Main-thread / Zustand secret
useSessionStore.setState({ mnemonic: words.join(" ") });
console.log("unlocked", mnemonic);
```

### GOOD

```ts
// Worker unlock only; UI gets public state
const publicState = await worker.unlockVault(password);
useSessionStore.getState().setUnlocked(publicState);
```
